{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Boggman","id":"860303482065256448","is_bot":0,"username":"boggman1"},"author_id":"860303482065256448","channel_id":"850808447003656242","content":"Thomas O'Malley is 6'2\", 220lbs, is of fit build with brown hair and grey eyes. The son of a tailor and a seamstress. He always felt stifled and claustrophobic in the city, but he didn't really understand why until his parents took him out into the surrounding forests for the first time. From then on he was one of those kids who constantly was going out into the woods and bringing home \"treasures\" like unique herbs and pieces of petrified wood, or -- on occasion -- a small animal (sometimes not so small) that he would smuggle into his room, and would inevitably escape to wreak havoc on the house at best, and the neighborhood at worst.\nWhen he was of age, he cheerfully gathered his things, bid his oft-exasperated parents farewell, and went off to live in the woods. He's not a stereotypical \"hippie\" druid, as he definitely eats meat and doesn't stress about killing things for food, because...that's how the natural world works. More of a mountain-man type of person that likes to live off the land and learn more about animals, especially since he found a book written by an ancient archdruid, with detailed drawings -- many so lifelike they almost seem to move upon the page -- and descriptions of the anatomy, behavior, and environment of many different species of natural animals. Written in Druidic, and therefore indecipherable to non-druids except via magic. He is unable to read all of it yet, not having fully unlocked its secrets. Now he is off to empire city to start his adventure in new lands","created_at":"2021-07-11T03:05:14.407000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"863616900927848508","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
