{"attachments":[{"content_type":"image/png","filename":"Dragheart_Luard-portrait.png","id":"863617405448224838","local_path":"discord/empire-city/attachments/850808447003656242/863617405448224838-Dragheart_Luard-portrait.png","message_id":"863617405704339466","sha256":"5d89844677080d40ff45b01373aab4217574b2a66fee55843410f65bec28ca89","size":1263195,"url":"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/850808447003656242/863617405448224838/Dragheart_Luard-portrait.png?ex=6ac07162&is=6abf1fe2&hm=987865bebd83f447eafe8af01fb6af6661b4f708405c2f23affe27a823630fb1&"}],"author":{"display_name":"unashaminglyme","id":"340062533304057857","is_bot":0,"username":"unashaminglyme"},"author_id":"340062533304057857","channel_id":"850808447003656242","content":"**__Description:__**\nLuard Dragonheart is an Aereni High Draconic Bloodline Sorcerer. He sports a 6’2” height topped with corn blonde long hair. He favors wearing elegant wizard robes along with a pointy wizard hat, all following his favorite color palette of purple and black.\nThanks to his rough childhood, Luard can be brash and abrasive and tends to give off a bad first impression. Thankfully, due to his noble heritage, Luard was taught how to socialize and could control his mean streak most of the time. His childhood lessons combined with his natural silver tongue makes Luard charming and cunningly deceptive. \nIn everything he does, Luard always pursues more power and magic knowledge, stopping at almost nothing to get what he wants; The power to prove his family’s disappointment in him wrong.\n\n**__Intro:__**\nLuard came from a long line of highly accomplished Aereni High Elf wizards, the Faranell nobles. Much was expected from Luard in his childhood and much he didn’t show. He had the hardest time grasping simple arcana and could not for the life of him cast the spells his relatives performed with ease. Life was hard and full of familial pressure for the young wizard. \nOne especially frustrating day, while Luard was trying his damndest to cast mage hand he realized why he couldn’t learn magic. Through sheer force of will, a splash of acid burst forth from Luard’s hands. The reason why he couldn’t learn magic was that magic was already in him, just waiting to be unleashed. Armed with the knowledge of his black dragon ancestry, Luard took on the new name of Dragonhear and left his family for greater adventures.\nLuard roamed the world for knowledge about dragons and magic. He wanted enough power to prove that his family’s years of disappointment and scorn for him was a massive mistake. And now, after half a year in Empire City’s Kingsbridge Noir, with the knowledge of living shadows and other strange magics, Luard just might be onto something.","created_at":"2021-07-11T03:07:14.755000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"863617405704339466","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
